// Title: OMeta: an object-oriented language for pattern matching
// Authors: Alessandro Warth, Ian Piumarta
// Source: VPRI Technical Report TR-2007-003 (2007), Figure 2 ("Flattening lists."). PDF page 5 (of 10), top.
// Transcribed from the page images; text-layer differences noted below.

meta F {
  flatten ::= (<inside>:xs)                 => xs;
  inside  ::= (<inside>:xs) <inside>:ys     => (append xs ys)
            | <_>:x         <inside>:xs     => (cons   x  xs)
            | <empty>                       => nil;
}

// Transcription notes
// - Checked at 300 dpi. Glyphs match the text layer.
// - Column spacing follows the page image to the nearest column; the second column of "=>" and the
//   right-hand alternatives are aligned as printed. Interior space runs may differ slightly.
// - Caption (not part of listing): "Flattening lists."
